<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling (Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold))",
        "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling faithfully reproduces Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/tero-physarum-transport-network-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py> ;
    schema:about "Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic mechanics, calcium oscillator or Alim et al. (2013) hydrodynamic-feedback generation of the contraction wave, random-network-peristalsis phase statistics, or a compliance model for volume closure",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 8-point gamma sweep in [0.8, 2.4] with TL_MST / MD_MST / FT / Betti-1 computed from the pruned graph (`compute_network_morphometrics`, fixed threshold D >= 0.10 max D) against the vendored reference table: TL r = 0.987 (RMSE 1.61), FT r = 0.848 (RMSE 0.178); gamma = 1.8: TL_MST 1.703, FT 0.745, MD_MST 0.796, Betti-1 8",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` (Betti-1 = 33 loops, 3-tier vein-width hierarchy, Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774, N = 17)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`, with a zero-sum `extra_sources` vector) across N_f = 36 food sources on a jittered 8x8 lattice; nodal conservation error < 1e-11 and flux antisymmetry < 1e-14",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Reduced two-timescale peristalsis: imposed plane wave rho_e(t) = 1 - eps cos(omega t - 2 pi x_e.n / lambda), instantaneous conductivity D_e rho_e^4, mean-corrected nodal volume source, Kirchhoff re-solved at 48 phases with D frozen; 1.70 reversals/cycle over active tubes (85.1 % reverse; eps = 0 ablation 0 / 0 %), osc/steady flux rms 0.697; pure-peristalsis wavelength sweep argmax lambda*/L = 1.5 (shallow, non-unique); eps sweep of the coupled pruning Betti-1 = [4, 5, 8, 27, 34, 71], Spearman rho = 1.0",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Two-path competition sweep (gamma = 0.6: Q1/I0 = 0.7322; gamma = 1.0, 1.8: 1.0000; gamma = 0 ablation 0.6667) and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 at gamma = 4/3",
        "reported_in_source: Alim et al. (2013) PNAS 110:13306-13311: actomyosin peristaltic contraction waves with period ~100 s and wavelength of order the organism size drive shuttle streaming (flow reversing twice per cycle) and a second-order net transport; Kamiya (1981): sinusoidal shuttle streaming reverses twice per contraction period",
        "reported_in_source: Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3",
        "reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij",
        "reported_in_source: Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network on a jittered 8x8 lattice (not Kanto geography) and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins",
        "transfer_boundary: The contraction wave is imposed (prescribed sinusoid along a fixed 20 deg direction, single wavelength), not generated by cortex mechanics or hydrodynamic feedback; T_c = 100 s is an input and 1/mu = 1800 s is an unsourced model-scale anchor, so only the 2-per-cycle phase locking, the second-order net transport and the eps-pruning coupling are model results",
        "transfer_boundary: eps = 0.0025 is a disclosed calibration chosen so that the gamma = 1.8 network lands in the Physarum TL_MST band; with eps = 0 the same model gives TL_MST = 1.149" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "6. Tip-Splitting & Flow Trees" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Bifurcating Vascular/Lung Trees" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Murray Law r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Slime Molds & Bacteria" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Physarum" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py; output: docs/media/physarum_transport_network_comparison.png; organism: Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/171769b9; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 9d2ad477cfb2fd69b34482f7554563764e14b823bf3616cc6b81b255bf0d40eb; artifact_sha256: 62ea6f63e161d275493b770aecf64e1191174f3c35bd7a93b7884d4d1a900657; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/physarum_transport_network/paper_citations.bib=b5e0e4eccbb78c29..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json=299541a0501eb573..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg=86a37f7c73c8527b..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json=4a54186a148929f7..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/scout_manifest.json=edb27b0addb825b3...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij | Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1 | Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3 | Alim et al. (2013) PNAS 110:13306-13311: actomyosin peristaltic contraction waves with period ~100 s and wavelength of order the organism size drive shuttle streaming (flow reversing twice per cycle) and a second-order net transport; Kamiya (1981): sinusoidal shuttle streaming reverses twice per contraction period; reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`, with a zero-sum `extra_sources` vector) across N_f = 36 food sources on a jittered 8x8 lattice; nodal conservation error < 1e-11 and flux antisymmetry < 1e-14 | 8-point gamma sweep in [0.8, 2.4] with TL_MST / MD_MST / FT / Betti-1 computed from the pruned graph (`compute_network_morphometrics`, fixed threshold D >= 0.10 max D) against the vendored reference table: TL r = 0.987 (RMSE 1.61), FT r = 0.848 (RMSE 0.178); gamma = 1.8: TL_MST 1.703, FT 0.745, MD_MST 0.796, Betti-1 8 | Reduced two-timescale peristalsis: imposed plane wave rho_e(t) = 1 - eps cos(omega t - 2 pi x_e.n / lambda), instantaneous conductivity D_e rho_e^4, mean-corrected nodal volume source, Kirchhoff re-solved at 48 phases with D frozen; 1.70 reversals/cycle over active tubes (85.1 % reverse; eps = 0 ablation 0 / 0 %), osc/steady flux rms 0.697; pure-peristalsis wavelength sweep argmax lambda*/L = 1.5 (shallow, non-unique); eps sweep of the coupled pruning Betti-1 = [4, 5, 8, 27, 34, 71], Spearman rho = 1.0 | Two-path competition sweep (gamma = 0.6: Q1/I0 = 0.7322; gamma = 1.0, 1.8: 1.0000; gamma = 0 ablation 0.6667) and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 at gamma = 4/3 | Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` (Betti-1 = 33 loops, 3-tier vein-width hierarchy, Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774, N = 17); transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network on a jittered 8x8 lattice (not Kanto geography) and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins | The contraction wave is imposed (prescribed sinusoid along a fixed 20 deg direction, single wavelength), not generated by cortex mechanics or hydrodynamic feedback; T_c = 100 s is an input and 1/mu = 1800 s is an unsourced model-scale anchor, so only the 2-per-cycle phase locking, the second-order net transport and the eps-pruning coupling are model results | eps = 0.0025 is a disclosed calibration chosen so that the gamma = 1.8 network lands in the Physarum TL_MST band; with eps = 0 the same model gives TL_MST = 1.149; does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic mechanics, calcium oscillator or Alim et al. (2013) hydrodynamic-feedback generation of the contraction wave, random-network-peristalsis phase statistics, or a compliance model for volume closure]" ;
