<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-L63) maps each of the four law groups to its equations, papers and Lean theorem with file#line pins; the Section 2b banner (L299-L336) states the reduced model, its assumptions and the calibration disclosure; every new function docstring names the quantity it returns; the math-KG YAML registers Laws 4-5 with single-range `code_locus` pins and `lean_locus`. Deductions: the Lean theorems are algebraic identities on Int (zero-sum of three mean-corrected sources, (g+d)dp + (g-d)(-dp) = 2 d dp) and do not formalise the Kirchhoff solvability or the O(eps) half-period antisymmetry that the comments attribute to them (-5); the \"Kamiya 1959\" / \"Kamiya 1981\" inconsistency (L301 vs the bib) (-1); measurement 1's note states a D1*/D2* that the code does not produce (L1556) (-3); the fixed PRUNING_THRESHOLD (L586) and the 0.55 initial conductivity (L530) carry no source (-2); the handoff-era inline comments documenting the v2 -> v3 change are credited (-3 net less)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_057_physarum_transport_network.lean L179–L227: Theorems 4-5 are Int identities (zero-sum, two-sample net flux); the half-period antisymmetry of the network flux is asserted only to O(eps) in Suite 8, not formalised <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_057_physarum_transport_network.lean#L179-L227>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The core Tero model is implemented faithfully: graph-Laplacian Kirchhoff solve with grounded sink (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`, L238-L295), sigmoidal reinforcement dD/dt = f(<|Q|>) - mu D on a multi-source network (L501-L583), two-path competition (L786-L836) and Murray's law at gamma = 4/3 (L866-L911), and the Pass 3 peristalsis layer is a coherent reduced model (wave geometry L349-L368, cycle solve with mean-corrected volume closure L371-L447, slow coupling through <|Q|> L550-L562) with Lean Theorems 4-5. Deductions: the prescribed closed-form TL/MD/FT curves that the v2 score of 95 relied on have been removed, and the genuine model does not reproduce the reference TL curve (RMSE 1.61, lattice saturates at TL ~ 6.8 for gamma = 0.8 vs 3.42) (-6); the contraction wave is imposed, not generated — no cortex / calcium oscillator or hydrodynamic feedback, fixed 20 deg plane wave (-4); feeding <|Q|> into f(.) swamps pruning for eps >~ 0.005 (FT -> 1, no shortest-path selection), so the biological regime where shuttle flow >> net flow AND pruning still happens is not reproduced (-4); source-sink pairs cycle by deterministic arithmetic (L541-L549) rather than Tero's random pair switching (-2); the \"Kanto\" graph is a jittered 8x8 lattice with a sinusoidal food-source selector (L163-L185), not geography (-2); MD_MST is normalised by a metric-closure MST (L221-L223) so MD_MST < 1 everywhere (0.43-0.80 vs ref 0.84-0.98), a definition mismatch with Tero (-2); volume closure is a uniform mean correction, not a compliance model (L416) (-1); Pass 3 credits (graph-computed statistics, honest ablations) prevent a larger fall." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L158–L235: 'Kanto' graph is a jittered 8x8 lattice; food sources chosen by distance to (3.5, 3.5) plus 0.15 sin(1.7x + 1.3y); no geographic data <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L158-L235>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Morphometric validation: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1529-L1690) now reports 14 metrics with method strings, RMSE / p-values and ablation controls, and the Pass 3 metrics each carry an eps = 0 null (reversals 0, fraction 0, net transport < 1e-12). Deductions: the v2 headline fits were against prescribed curves; the honest graph-computed TL has RMSE 1.61 against the reference table and FT r = 0.848 (RMSE 0.178), with a non-monotone FT tail at gamma = 2.4 caused by conditioning on connected pairs (L488-L497) (-8); the gamma = 1.8 TL_MST = 1.703 \"match\" to 1.75 depends on the eps = 0.0025 calibration (eps = 0 gives 1.149), disclosed at L333-L338 but still a calibration landing on the target (-6); specimen reference values 0.8926 (L1634) and 33 (L1624) are the script's own earlier outputs (circular) (-4); measurement 1 compares the sigmoid-kernel run (L853) with the power-law analytical reference 0.7401 and its note still claims D1*/D2* = 2.83 while the run gives 1.367 (L1556) (-3); peristalsis references are definitional (2 reversals), qualitative (1.0) or recalled (lambda/L = 1, T_c = 100 s), and two metrics have reference_value None (-5); MD_MST (0.796 vs 0.85) is reported only inside a method string, not as a scored metric (-2); self-test thresholds were relaxed to r_TL > 0.90 / r_FT > 0.75 to admit the honest values (L1731-L1732) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L1549–L1558: Measurement 1: sigmoid-kernel run (sublinear_06, power_law_kernel=False at L853) compared with the power-law analytical 0.7401; note claims D1*/D2* = 2.8284 while the run reports 1.367 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L1549-L1558>",
        "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L1619–L1638: Specimen Betti-1 reference 33 and Murray reference 0.8926 are the script's own prior outputs — circular reference_value <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L1619-L1638>",
        "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L1728–L1740: Suite 5 thresholds relaxed to r_TL > 0.90, r_FT > 0.75 and monotone TL to admit the graph-computed values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L1728-L1740>" ;
