<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — MorphoEval overall 80.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py`. The one open v2 item is closed as a reduced, honestly-labelled two-timescale model: an imposed actomyosin plane wave modulates every tube's conductivity (D_e rho_e^4) and injects a zero-sum nodal volume source into the Kirchhoff Laplacian; the quasi-static cycle reproduces shuttle streaming (1.70 reversals/cycle over active tubes, 85 % of tubes reverse, 0 in the eps = 0 ablation), a second-order net peristaltic transport that vanishes for frozen conductance (Lean Theorem 5), and a monotone feedback of contraction amplitude on long-timescale pruning (Betti-1 4 -> 71 across eps 0 -> 0.01, Spearman rho = 1.0). Pass 3 also removed the v2 prescribed TL/MD/FT sigmoids; the Fig. 3 statistics are now graph-computed and the honest agreement is weaker (TL r = 0.987 but RMSE 1.61 because the dense lattice saturates at low gamma; FT r = 0.848). The overall score falls from 93.4 because the v2 score rested on prescribed curves and because the new layer exposes: an eps default calibrated to the Physarum TL band, an unsourced 1800 s adaptation time, a Fig. 3 reference table of unverified digitisation, circular specimen references (0.8926, 33), definitional/recalled peristalsis references, two unverified DOIs, a jittered lattice labelled as Kanto, deterministic source-sink pairing, and MD_MST / FT definitions that differ from Tero's. Overall 80.4/100 (faithfulness 78.1, reproducibility 85.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 171769b9; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 80, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/physarum_transport_network_comparison.png: rendered output of 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py at 171769b9, image/png, 1759411 B, 2610×2340 px, artifact_sha256 62ea6f63e161d275493b770aecf64e1191174f3c35bd7a93b7884d4d1a900657 (sha256 62ea6f63e161d275493b770aecf64e1191174f3c35bd7a93b7884d4d1a900657), spec_fingerprint 9d2ad477cfb2fd69b34482f7554563764e14b823bf3616cc6b81b255bf0d40eb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9d2ad477cfb2fd69b34482f7554563764e14b823bf3616cc6b81b255bf0d40eb; artifact_sha256: 62ea6f63e161d275493b770aecf64e1191174f3c35bd7a93b7884d4d1a900657; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/physarum_transport_network/paper_citations.bib=b5e0e4eccbb78c29..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json=299541a0501eb573..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg=86a37f7c73c8527b..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json=4a54186a148929f7..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/scout_manifest.json=edb27b0addb825b3...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij | Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1 | Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3 | Alim et al. (2013) PNAS 110:13306-13311: actomyosin peristaltic contraction waves with period ~100 s and wavelength of order the organism size drive shuttle streaming (flow reversing twice per cycle) and a second-order net transport; Kamiya (1981): sinusoidal shuttle streaming reverses twice per contraction period; reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`, with a zero-sum `extra_sources` vector) across N_f = 36 food sources on a jittered 8x8 lattice; nodal conservation error < 1e-11 and flux antisymmetry < 1e-14 | 8-point gamma sweep in [0.8, 2.4] with TL_MST / MD_MST / FT / Betti-1 computed from the pruned graph (`compute_network_morphometrics`, fixed threshold D >= 0.10 max D) against the vendored reference table: TL r = 0.987 (RMSE 1.61), FT r = 0.848 (RMSE 0.178); gamma = 1.8: TL_MST 1.703, FT 0.745, MD_MST 0.796, Betti-1 8 | Reduced two-timescale peristalsis: imposed plane wave rho_e(t) = 1 - eps cos(omega t - 2 pi x_e.n / lambda), instantaneous conductivity D_e rho_e^4, mean-corrected nodal volume source, Kirchhoff re-solved at 48 phases with D frozen; 1.70 reversals/cycle over active tubes (85.1 % reverse; eps = 0 ablation 0 / 0 %), osc/steady flux rms 0.697; pure-peristalsis wavelength sweep argmax lambda*/L = 1.5 (shallow, non-unique); eps sweep of the coupled pruning Betti-1 = [4, 5, 8, 27, 34, 71], Spearman rho = 1.0 | Two-path competition sweep (gamma = 0.6: Q1/I0 = 0.7322; gamma = 1.0, 1.8: 1.0000; gamma = 0 ablation 0.6667) and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 at gamma = 4/3 | Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` (Betti-1 = 33 loops, 3-tier vein-width hierarchy, Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774, N = 17); transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network on a jittered 8x8 lattice (not Kanto geography) and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins | The contraction wave is imposed (prescribed sinusoid along a fixed 20 deg direction, single wavelength), not generated by cortex mechanics or hydrodynamic feedback; T_c = 100 s is an input and 1/mu = 1800 s is an unsourced model-scale anchor, so only the 2-per-cycle phase locking, the second-order net transport and the eps-pruning coupling are model results | eps = 0.0025 is a disclosed calibration chosen so that the gamma = 1.8 network lands in the Physarum TL_MST band; with eps = 0 the same model gives TL_MST = 1.149; does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic mechanics, calcium oscillator or Alim et al. (2013) hydrodynamic-feedback generation of the contraction wave, random-network-peristalsis phase statistics, or a compliance model for volume closure." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:158-185 — the graph is a jittered 8x8 lattice with a sinusoidal food-source selector; Panel A labels it \"Kanto West-East coordinate\" with a \"Tokyo\" hub. Either vendor the Tero 2010 station coordinates (Fig. 1) or relabel the panel and docstrings as a synthetic lattice.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:1619-1638 — specimen reference values 33 (Betti-1) and 0.8926 (Murray ratio) are the script's own earlier outputs. Replace with an independent anchor (e.g. a manual count on the specimen recorded in the dataset README, or a published Physarum junction-ratio range) or set reference_value to null and say so.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:301 — Section 2b banner cites \"Kamiya 1959\" while the bib, JSON and measurement sources cite Kamiya (1981); unify, and verify both the Kamiya (1981) and Alim (2013) DOIs once network access is available (flag remains `doi_verified_offline: false`).",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:333-338 and 343 — eps = 0.0025 is a calibration that lands TL_MST(gamma = 1.8) in the Physarum band (eps = 0 gives 1.149) and ADAPTATION_TIME_S = 1800 s is unsourced; together they set the osc/steady flux ratio. Fix eps from a measured relative radius amplitude (Alim et al. 2013 report tube-radius oscillation amplitudes) and 1/mu from a sourced adaptation timescale, vendor both with DOI-level provenance, and re-report TL_MST without a target-landing choice.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:349-368 and 371-447 — the contraction wave is imposed (fixed 20 deg plane wave, prescribed sinusoid). Replace or supplement with a generated wave (e.g. a phase-oscillator field on the nodes with nearest-neighbour coupling, or the Alim et al. hydrodynamic feedback) so that wave direction and wavelength are outputs; expose direction / lambda / T_c on the CLI.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:488-497 and 482-486 — FT is conditioned on currently connected food-source pairs (non-monotone tail: FT(2.4) = 0.60 > FT(2.1) = 0.53 while the network is fragmented) and MD_MST is normalised by a metric-closure MST so MD_MST < 1 everywhere. Use Tero's definitions (FT counts disconnection of any food source; MST built on the same lattice) or report FT only for connected networks.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:550-562 and 731-750 — feeding <|Q|> into f(.) suppresses pruning for eps >~ 0.005 (FT -> 1, Betti-1 71), so the regime where shuttle flow >> net flow AND the network still selects short paths is not reproduced. Implement an alternative shear read-out (rectified net component <Q>, or amplitude-relative |Q| - <|Q|>_network) and show which read-out keeps Tero pruning under strong peristalsis.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:718-729 — the lambda/L optimum is shallow and non-unique (1.5 and 2.0 tie at 0.014, 0.25 gives 0.013 on a 64-node graph); refine the lattice or report the plateau width instead of a single argmax, and do not present measurement 13 as confirming Alim's lambda ~ L.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py:853 and 1549-1558 — measurement 1 compares the sigmoid-kernel gamma = 0.6 run with the power-law analytical 0.7401 and its note claims D1*/D2* = 2.8284 while the run gives 1.367. Either run `sublinear_06` with power_law_kernel=True (then 0.7401 is the correct reference) or derive the sigmoid fixed point and update the note.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json (gamma_phase_transition_sweep table and Tokyo/Physarum benchmarks) — not traceable to a digitisation; Tero 2010 Fig. 3 plots statistics against I0 for several gamma. Re-digitise the actual figure (with I0 axis) or relabel the table as a reconstruction and drop the Pearson-r framing in measurements 3-4." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.04e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Sweeps: 8 gamma values on the multi-source network (L597-L678), 19 gamma values plus gamma = 0 ablation on the two-path circuit (L839-L858), 7 flux splits for Murray (L866-L911), and new in Pass 3 a 9-point wavelength sweep lambda/L in [0.25, 8] (L718-L729) and a 6-point eps sweep of the coupled pruning (L731-L750); CLI exposes --gamma, --i0, --mu, --seed and the new --peristalsis-eps (L1813-L1822), and the dead --gamma flag now actually changes the rendered network (L1055-L1067). Deductions: wave direction (20 deg), T_c, lambda/L and the phase-sample counts are module constants with no CLI (L340-L346) (-5); --i0 / --mu reach only the shown network and the Murray check while the gamma sweep and all measurements always run at defaults (L1046, L1517-L1522 area) (-4); `seed` only jitters node coordinates because pairing is deterministic (-2); the eps sweep stops at 0.01 so the regime where every tube reverses (eps >= 0.05, Suite 8) is tested but not shown in Panel I (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L338–L346: DEFAULT_PERISTALSIS_EPS, sweeps, wavelength ratio, T_c, ADAPTATION_TIME_S, wave direction and phase counts are constants without CLI exposure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L338-L346>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-parameter-expressivity-1>,
