        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` runs 11 suites in ~7 s (SHA-256 of 3 files, Kirchhoff conservation, two-path transition, gamma = 0 ablation, graph-computed sweep with bitwise eps = 0 determinism, Murray, specimen CV, peristaltic closure < 1e-12 / reversal / exact 2-per-cycle at eps = 0.05 / O(eps) antisymmetry, second-order transport with a linear null < 1e-12, eps monotonicity, 14-metric bitwise determinism); the default render takes ~6.5 s and writes the PNG and both GIFs; `measure_morphoeval()` accepts a shared results bundle so nothing is computed twice. Deductions: the PNG is gitignored (`*.png`) so the audited figure is not in the repository and must be regenerated (-3); Suite 5 thresholds were loosened to admit the honest values rather than tightened (-2); no requirements lock pins the environment (versions recorded only in this audit) (-3); the self-test's compute_all_results() call is repeated by measure_morphoeval() in Suite 11, so the suite runs the full pipeline twice (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Source and data traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Three vendored inputs are SHA-256-verified at every run (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L112-L150, including the new `peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json`), the bib has 7 entries, the dataset README has a Pass 3 section (L32-L44) and the new JSON carries explicit `value_provenance` and a `provenance_note`. Deductions: the Kamiya (1981) DOI and the Alim (2013) DOI could not be verified offline and the JSON values T_c = 100 s and lambda*/L = 1 are `recalled` (L6, L30-L36, L52-L58) (-6); `ADAPTATION_TIME_S = 1800 s` (L343), which fixes omega and therefore the absolute shuttle-flux scale, is marked \"unsourced\" (-5); the pre-existing Fig. 3 reference table (8 gamma points with TL/MD/FT/Betti-1) and the Tokyo / Physarum benchmark numbers are not traceable to a specific digitisation — Tero 2010 Fig. 3 plots statistics against I0 for several gamma, not an 8-point gamma scan — so measurements 3-6 are against a reconstruction (-6); the Section 2b banner cites \"Kamiya 1959\" (L301) while the bib and JSON cite Kamiya 1981 (-1); the eps calibration disclosure is credited (+2 net against a larger deduction)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L343–L343: ADAPTATION_TIME_S = 1800 s labelled 'model-scale anchor, unsourced' — sets omega and the osc/steady flux ratio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L343-L343>",
        "datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json L1–L186: Pre-existing gamma_phase_transition_sweep_tero2010_fig3 table and Tokyo/Physarum benchmarks without digitisation provenance (Pass 1 reconstruction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json#L1-L186>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
