<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-pinned specimen photograph is still segmented into 33 loops with a 3-tier vein hierarchy and Y-junction Murray ratios (`segment_physarum_specimen`, L919-L1025), and the figure now adds the shuttle-streaming time series with ablation (Panel G), net transport vs lambda/L with the Alim line (H), and the eps sweep against the Physarum TL band (I) plus a 24-frame signed-flux GIF. Deductions: the simulated network is a jittered lattice yet Panel A labels its axis \"Kanto West-East coordinate\" and calls the central node Tokyo (L158-L185) (-5); the specimen Betti-1 = 33 and Murray 0.8926 references are the script's own earlier outputs, so \"match\" here is self-agreement (-5); the shuttle-streaming comparison is to definitional / qualitative anchors (2 reversals, \"all tubes oscillate\"), not to a vendored flow-velocity trace or to Alim et al. kymographs (-5); 15 % of trunk tubes keep a steady bias at the default eps, which is reported honestly (-2); the Panel H optimum is shallow and non-unique (1.5 and 2.0 tie at 0.014; 0.25 gives 0.013) and should not be read as confirming lambda ~ L (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json L30–L63: Reference anchors are value_provenance 'recalled' (T_c, lambda/L), 'definitional' (2 reversals) and 'qualitative' (fraction reversing) — weak specimen anchors <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json#L30-L63>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-2>,
